{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.delta_pre_archimedean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.delta_pre_archimedean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.archimedean_does_not_commute_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.archimedean_does_not_commute_sub","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L72-L88","doc":"**The archimedean realisation does NOT commute with the delta.** A\nnonlinear `τ` (here squaring, standing in for the Li_2^q-tower /\nproduct / 𝔈₀-scaling structure of the real archimedean realisation)\nsatisfies `τ(xn) − τ(xp) ≠ τ(xn − xp)` in general. We exhibit a\nconcrete witness over `ℤ`: with `τ = (·)²`, `xn = 2`, `xp = 1`,\n`τ(2) − τ(1) = 3` but `τ(2 − 1) = 1`.\n\nConsequence: the masses-then-delta order (`τ xn − τ xp`) is NOT\nequal to, and NOT fold-invariant like, the delta-then-archimedean\norder (`τ (xn − xp)`). The framework computes Q_β / binding in the\ndelta-then-archimedean order precisely so the fold discipline and\nthe difference structure are preserved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.fold_commutes_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.fold_commutes_sub","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L62-L70","doc":"**Fold commutes with the categorical delta.** For a fibre fold `f`\nand fibre quantities `x_n, x_p`,\n`f(x_n − x_p) = f(x_n) − f(x_p)`.\nThe fold can be applied on either side of the pre-archimedean\nsubtraction — this is what makes folding/unfolding legitimate for\nthe difference observables (binding energy, Q_β). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:delta-pre-archimedean","label":"prop:delta-pre-archimedean","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/delta-pre-archimedean.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.map_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.map_neg","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L55-L60","doc":"An additive map sends negation to negation: `fold(−x) = −fold(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.map_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.map_zero","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.map_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.map_add","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.toFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.toFun","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FibreFold","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/delta_pre_archimedean.lean#L46-L53","doc":"A **fibre fold** is any additive map on the coefficient ring (the\nbar involution `q↦q⁻¹`, the Hecke antipode `σ↦σ⁻¹`, a Type-B fold —\nall are ring homomorphisms, in particular additive). We capture the\nonly property the delta argument needs: additivity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}